{"reference":"1 Samuel 21","book":"1 Samuel","chapter":21,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Within First Samuel","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"This chapter belongs to First Samuel’s larger movement from Eli’s failing priestly house, through Samuel’s leadership and Saul’s rejected kingship, to David’s anointing, rise, and exile. David’s flight from Saul here is part of that wider account.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_samuel_021_8007d9eb1979ebd595774df7"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}